From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:21:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] proc: a context killed before it ever ran exits in the kernel

A context made through "new-context" starts with an empty kernel
function and then enters user space with the registers user space set.
When it was force-killed before anyone set them up, it entered user
space with all registers zero and died of an unhandled exception at
PC 0, with a register dump in the log, and procmgr saw an exception
exit instead of SIGKILL.

redox-rt does this on purpose since redox-rpi#707: when a fork fails
after procmgr created the child, it force-kills the child's thread.
The first kernel function now checks being_sigkilled and exits the
context there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/scheme/proc.rs | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/scheme/proc.rs b/src/scheme/proc.rs
index 1b817110..7f9acf7f 100644
--- a/src/scheme/proc.rs
+++ b/src/scheme/proc.rs
@@ -309,7 +309,20 @@ impl ProcScheme {
                 }
             },
             OpenTy::Auth => {
-                extern "C" fn ret() {}
+                // First kernel code of a new context, run before it enters user space. A
+                // context that was force-killed before it ever ran (redox-rt kills the child
+                // of a fork that failed half-way, redox-rpi#707) exits here, instead of
+                // entering user space with zeroed registers and dying of an exception at PC 0.
+                extern "C" fn ret() {
+                    if crate::percpu::PercpuBlock::current()
+                        .switch_internals
+                        .being_sigkilled
+                        .get()
+                    {
+                        let mut token = unsafe { CleanLockToken::new() };
+                        crate::syscall::process::exit_this_context(None, &mut token);
+                    }
+                }
                 let context = match operation_str.ok_or(Error::new(ENOENT))? {
                     "new-context" => {
                         let id = NonZeroUsize::new(NEXT_ID.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed))
-- 
